            <ArticleTitle>Physiologic signs and symptoms: contribution to the interpretation of the exercise test.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>355-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Evaluation of the physiologic responses to exercise can greatly enhance the information gained by consideration of the electrocardiogram alone. Interpretation of chest pain patterns, blood pressure and heart rate responses, and changing physical examinations is essential for complete interpretation of the exercise stress test.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
